---
import '../styles/global.css';
const github = 'https://github.com/sidneykanoti/LNMTLWebToEbook';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="Download whole novels listed on lnmtl.com and preserve them as EPUB, PDF, or HTML. Free independent desktop downloader for Windows, macOS, and Linux. Not affiliated with lnmtl.com." />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#123f36" />
    <title>LNMTL Web to Ebook — Preserve the novels you love.</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="/app-icon.png" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="nav wrap">
      <a class="brand" href="#" aria-label="LNMTL Web to Ebook home"><img src="/app-icon.png" alt="" width="40" height="40" /><span>LNMTL <small>Web to Ebook</small></span></a>
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="#why">Why preserve?</a><a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a><a href="#questions">FAQs</a><a class="nav-download" href="#download">Get the app <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></nav>
    </header>
    <main>
      <section class="hero wrap">
        <div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> AN INDEPENDENT NOVEL DOWNLOADER</p><h1>Keep the novels.<br /><em>Keep the stories.</em></h1><p class="intro">Download whole novels listed on lnmtl.com and preserve them on your computer as EPUB, PDF, or HTML. Built to help readers keep the stories they love before they become unavailable.</p><a class="button" id="hero-download" href="#download">Get the free app <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><p class="micro">Windows, macOS & Linux · Free to use</p><p class="independence">Independent software by Sidney Kanoti. Not affiliated with lnmtl.com.</p></div>
        <div class="book-scene" aria-label="EPUB, PDF and HTML books for offline reading"><div class="scene-ring"></div><span class="scene-note">Your novels. Preserved.</span><div class="book book-back"><span>THE OFFLINE<br />COLLECTION</span><i>HTML · PDF</i></div><div class="book book-front"><span class="book-top">YOUR PERSONAL NOVEL ARCHIVE</span><div class="book-line"></div><strong>Keep the<br />whole<br /><em>story.</em></strong><span class="book-bottom">PRESERVED FOR ANOTHER DAY<br /><b>EPUB / PDF / HTML</b></span></div><span class="scene-caption">Stories worth keeping.</span></div>
      </section>
      <div class="format-strip"><div class="wrap"><span>Whole novels. Your own library.</span><span>EPUB <i>For your ebook reader</i></span><span>PDF <i>For familiar pages</i></span><span>HTML <i>For your browser</i></span></div></div>
      <section class="mission wrap" id="why"><div><p class="eyebrow">WHY THIS PROJECT EXISTS</p><h2>A home for stories.<br /><em>Beyond a website.</em></h2></div><div class="mission-copy"><p class="mission-lead">LNMTL Web to Ebook was created to help preserve the novel content on lnmtl.com as its future becomes uncertain.</p><p>As the creator of this tool, I believe LNMTL is heading toward shutdown. My concern comes from what I see as a loss of motivation from the site owner to evolve the site, and the rise of AI making legacy machine-translation systems redundant.</p><p>Rather than risk losing access to the novels readers care about, I built a simple desktop downloader for saving whole novels into a personal library.</p><p class="mission-note">— Sidney Kanoti, project creator. This is the motivation behind this independent project, not an official shutdown announcement from lnmtl.com.</p></div></section>
      <section class="showcase wrap" id="inside"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">CHOOSE A NOVEL. DOWNLOAD ITS AVAILABLE CONTENT.</p><h2>Whole novels.<br /><em>One download job.</em></h2></div><p>Choose a novel and let the app download all of its available chapters, then export it as a book. You select novels, not individual chapters. Your library and download progress stay on your computer.</p></div><div class="app-frame"><div class="frame-bar"><span><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>LNMTL Web to Ebook</span><span>DESKTOP APP</span></div><a href="/app-screenshot.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Open full-size app screenshot"><img src="/app-screenshot.png" alt="LNMTL Web to Ebook desktop app with novel catalogue, search, download controls and EPUB, PDF and HTML export options" width="1327" height="990" loading="lazy" /></a></div><div class="feature-row"><div><span>01 / KEEP YOUR PLACE</span><h3>Resume a novel download.</h3><p>Pause a novel download and continue later. The app remembers its progress and skips content already saved, even after you close it.</p></div><div><span>02 / READ YOUR WAY</span><h3>A book in your favourite format.</h3><p>Export EPUB, PDF, or HTML. Keep the familiar light reading style, with chapter contents and volume headings.</p></div><div><span>03 / KEEP IT CLOSE</span><h3>Your library lives with you.</h3><p>Choose your library folder, keep your books locally, and read offline. No account or cloud upload required.</p></div></div></section>
      <section class="steps-section" id="how-it-works"><div class="wrap steps-layout"><div><p class="eyebrow">FROM NOVEL TO PERSONAL ARCHIVE</p><h2>Choose it.<br /><em>Preserve it.</em></h2><p>A workflow built around whole novels.</p></div><ol class="steps"><li><span>01</span><div><h3>Download and open.</h3><p>Choose the app for your computer. Everything you need to run the app is bundled in the release.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h3>Choose the novel to preserve.</h3><p>Paste a novel link or short name. Or click <b>Load catalogue</b> to list all LNMTL novels, then search for the one you want.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h3>Download the novel. Export your book.</h3><p>Select your novel, turn off <b>Sample first</b>, and click <b>Download / resume selected</b> to download all its indexed chapters. Choose EPUB, PDF, or HTML, then <b>Export selected</b>.</p><p class="tip">Whole-novel downloads require Sample first to be off. A complete download includes everything available and indexed on LNMTL; the source novel itself may still be unfinished or have missing chapters.</p></div></li></ol></div></section>
      <section class="download-section wrap" id="download"><p class="eyebrow">START YOUR PERSONAL NOVEL ARCHIVE</p><h2>Keep your novels.<br /><em>Read them offline.</em></h2><p>Free to use. Choose your computer below.</p><p id="download-error" role="alert" hidden>We couldn’t get the latest download right now. Please try again or <a href={`${github}/releases/latest`}>download from GitHub Releases</a>.</p><div class="downloads"><article data-os="windows"><span class="os-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⊞</span><h3>Windows</h3><p>Windows · 64-bit</p><a class="button" href="/download/windows">Download for Windows <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><small>Open the .exe to get started.</small></article><article data-os="mac"><span class="os-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⌘</span><h3>macOS</h3><p>Choose your Mac’s chip</p><a class="button" href="/download/mac-arm">Apple Silicon <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="secondary-download" href="/download/mac-intel">Download for Intel Mac ↓</a><small>Find your chip in About This Mac.</small></article><article data-os="linux"><span class="os-symbol" aria-hidden="true">&gt;_</span><h3>Linux</h3><p>Ubuntu 24.04+ · 64-bit</p><a class="button" href="/download/linux">Download for Linux <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="secondary-download" href="/download/linux-deb">Prefer a .deb package? ↓</a><small>Extract the archive and open the app.</small></article></div><p class="release-note">Always the latest release, directly from GitHub. <a href={`${github}/releases`}>View release notes ↗</a></p></section>
      <section class="faq wrap" id="questions"><div><p class="eyebrow">BEFORE YOU TURN THE PAGE</p><h2>A few good<br /><em>questions.</em></h2></div><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Is this an official LNMTL app?</summary><p>No. LNMTL Web to Ebook is an independent downloader for novels listed on <a href="https://lnmtl.com">lnmtl.com</a>. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or operated by lnmtl.com. Think of it as a download client: the software helps you save content from the source site to your own computer. It does not use BitTorrent or peer-to-peer sharing.</p></details><details><summary>Can I choose individual chapters?</summary><p>No. You choose novels, and the app downloads their available indexed chapters as a whole-novel job. There is no individual chapter picker. Turn off Sample first to download the full available novel rather than a sample.</p></details><details><summary>Is it really free?</summary><p>Yes. All features are free to use. If the app becomes part of your reading routine, you can optionally <a href="https://www.paypal.biz/omnipotentcore">support the project</a>.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need Python or other software?</summary><p>No. Download a packaged release for your computer. Python and the PDF engine are included. See the <a href={`${github}/blob/main/docs/USER_GUIDE.md`}>user guide</a> for platform-specific help.</p></details><details><summary>How do I download the whole novel?</summary><p>Sample first is enabled by default and saves three new chapters per run. Turn it off, select your novel, then click Download / resume selected. The app downloads all remaining indexed chapters. Export when the download finishes to create your book.</p></details><details><summary>Can I continue a download later?</summary><p>Yes. Your progress is kept locally. Reopen the app and resume; chapters already saved are skipped. Refresh the novel index to find newly available chapters.</p></details><details><summary>What if my computer shows a security prompt?</summary><p>The releases are not currently signed or notarized, so your operating system may show a warning. Read the <a href={`${github}/blob/main/PACKAGING.md`}>platform instructions</a> before opening the app if you encounter a prompt.</p></details><details><summary>Does it translate novels or work without internet?</summary><p>The app downloads the available English novel content from lnmtl.com; it does not translate new text. You need internet and an accessible source site to download novels. Exported books can be read offline. It cannot retrieve content that is no longer available on the source site.</p></details></div></section>
      <section class="support wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">BUILT TO HELP STORIES LAST</p><h3>Help keep the preservation tool going.</h3><p>Support the independent software behind your personal novel archive.</p></div><a class="outline-button" href="https://www.paypal.biz/omnipotentcore" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Support the project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
    </main>
    <footer class="wrap"><a class="brand" href="#"><img src="/app-icon.png" width="32" height="32" alt="" /><span>LNMTL <small>Web to Ebook</small></span></a><p>An independent project by Sidney Kanoti.<br />Not affiliated with lnmtl.com. Software licensed under GPL-3.0-only.</p><div><a href={github}>GitHub ↗</a><a href={`${github}/blob/main/docs/USER_GUIDE.md`}>User guide ↗</a></div></footer>
    <script>
      const platform = navigator.userAgent.toLowerCase();
      const os = /android|iphone|ipad/.test(platform) ? null : /win/.test(platform) ? 'windows' : /mac/.test(platform) ? 'mac' : /linux/.test(platform) ? 'linux' : null;
      if (os) {
        const card = document.querySelector(`[data-os="${os}"]`);
        card?.classList.add('recommended');
        const badge = document.createElement('span'); badge.className = 'recommended-label'; badge.textContent = 'FOR YOUR COMPUTER'; card?.prepend(badge);
        const button = document.querySelector<HTMLAnchorElement>('#hero-download');
        if (button) { button.textContent = os === 'mac' ? 'Choose your Mac download ↓' : `Download for ${os === 'windows' ? 'Windows' : 'Linux'} ↓`; button.href = os === 'mac' ? '#download' : `/download/${os}`; }
      }
      if (new URLSearchParams(location.search).has('download')) document.querySelector('#download-error')?.removeAttribute('hidden');
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
